<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The guild war score boards (uiguild.py GuildWarScoreBoard): one board
	     per war at the bottom left, each the two guilds' marks, names and
	     scores (and their member counts once the server sends them). While
	     the guild-war flag is on, the Interface makes one facade per war,
	     nui_guild_war.GuildWarScoreBoard (controller
	     assets/root/nui_guild_war.py), and every war is an entry of this one
	     document. Legacy puts every board at the same place, so a second war
	     hid the first; here they stack upward 4dp apart (spec D19). A mark is
	     a 16 x 12 region of the guild mark atlas the client downloads
	     (mark/<prefix>_<n>.tga), absent for a guild without one. A
	     full-screen overlay that takes no pointer and no focus. The classic
	     thin board art is under d:/ymir work/ (assets/ETC). Each repeated
	     slot binds nothing: RmlUi updates a repeated element's own views with
	     the data-for that removes it. -->
	<title>guild-war</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="guild-war.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="nui-overlay nui-below-legacy-ui guild-war" data-model="guild_war">
	<div id="guild-war" class="guild-war__column">
		<div class="guild-war__slot" data-for="b : boards">
			<div class="nui-panel guild-war__board" data-attr-id="'guild-war-' + b.key">
				<div class="guild-war__row-slot" data-for="row : b.rows">
					<div class="guild-war__row">
						<img class="guild-war__mark" data-if="row.src != ''" data-attr-src="row.src" data-attr-rect="row.rect"/>
						<span class="guild-war__text">{{ row.text }}</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
